all.\n\nThe cost is latency. Session reads are expected to rise from about 1ms to about 4ms at p99, which fits within our 200ms page budget.\n\nThe rollout has three phases. We dual-write for two weeks, then switch reads to Postgres, then remove Redis.\n\nThis change should improve reliability because sessions would no longer depend on a single node.","ttft_ms":2717,"type":"result","duration_ms":2737,"uuid":"bae188d9-19ec-4985-b4a1-6eff39dd569d","ttft_stream_ms":1248,"time_to_request_ms":18,"first_content_frame_ms":1248,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
